docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R55-contract-memory-verification-retrieval.md:37:- **No leak into `trusted`.** A `HashSet<String>` collects every `bundle.trusted.memory_id.ulid`; the test asserts that none of the five seeded ids appears in it. This is the §Non-Negotiable Product Properties guard ("Every stale or contradicted memory is surfaced as such, not hidden behind recency.") at the contract level — the test calls the production `partition` function, not a test double.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R55-contract-memory-verification-retrieval.md:39:- **Non-empty `label_reason`.** Each advisory entry must carry `!advisory.label_reason.trim().is_empty()`. This satisfies §Non-Negotiable Product Properties "Every retrieved memory has an inclusion reason" at the surfacing boundary.
