docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R78-frontend.md:249:The two file-size violations (F-1, F-2) and four function-length violations (F-3) are real but represent code-organization debt, not correctness or security risk — the file functions correctly under the existing test coverage. They are recorded in `T-followup-R78-A` and MUST be cleaned up before any Phase 11 task touches `reviewPanel.ts` or `rpcBridge.ts`, because the next session will breach the limit on first touch. The pagination + loading-skeleton gaps (F-4, F-5) and the error-handling tightening (F-6, F-9) are recorded in `T-followup-R78-B` and `T-followup-R78-C` respectively. None of the findings block downstream review tasks R79 or R88 from beginning.
