docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/R79.md:12:This review is the contract gate between the Phase 10 review UI and the daemon MCP surface that powers it. Every method on `ReviewRpcBridge` calls a tool registered on the daemon side; this gate verifies that every method has a matching tool, that the JSON shapes round-trip end to end, that the schema is documented and regression-tested, and that no surface added by Phases 6–9 was forgotten on the extension side. The gate exists because UI compile + lint cannot detect contract drift — only an integration test that sends a real request to a real daemon and asserts the response shape can. Spec §Non-Negotiable Product Properties demands "every public MCP contract is documented and regression-tested"; this review enforces that for the review UI surface.
