docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T81.md:1:# T81 — Phase 11 — Concurrency tests (parallel sessions, write contention, replay-safe)
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T81.md:7:**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 11: Hardening](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-11-hardening), [§3. Event Log](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#3-event-log), [§6. Consolidation Engine](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#6-consolidation-engine), [§Testing Requirements](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#testing-requirements)
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T81.md:12:This task delivers the concurrency test suite covering parallel sessions, write contention against the event log and memory store, and the replay-safe execution invariant for consolidation jobs. Spec §3 makes the event log append-only and replayable; spec §6 requires consolidation to be "auditable, reversible, and test-covered" with "replay-safe job execution." Spec §Phase 11 deliverables list "concurrency tests" explicitly. Without this suite, race conditions in event ordering, double-applied consolidation jobs, or memory-link torn writes would only surface in production. This task forces those failure modes to happen in CI.
