docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T57.md:12:This task redesigns the four discovery workflow tools (`get_context_capsule`, `get_docs_capsule`, `find_relevant_tests`, `impact_from_diff`) on top of the Phase 1–7 substrates so that each tool returns a compact bundle by default with deliberate expansion handles, rather than dumping broad slices of files. Spec §Non-Negotiable Product Properties requires "every workflow bundle is compact by default with deliberate expansion handles" and spec §Phase 8 DoD requires workflows that "produce enough context to implement and verify changes without broad file dumping." Without this redesign, discovery calls remain the dominant tool-call cost in Phase 9 metrics and the success criterion "40 percent fewer irrelevant file reads" cannot be met.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T57.md:16:> "Every workflow bundle is compact by default with deliberate expansion handles." (spec §Non-Negotiable Product Properties)
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T57.md:43:4. Implement `find_relevant_tests` in `workflow_v2/relevant_tests.rs`: accept either a file/symbol set or a diff, traverse `tested_by` edges in the Phase 1 graph, combine with `co_changed_with` evidence from the event log, score by graph proximity + past test-failure frequency, and return ranked test files with the verification command needed to run each (e.g. `cargo test -p X --lib mod::tests::test_name`). Spec §Measurable Success Criteria targets 90 percent correct relevant-test recommendation on curated tasks — the API must record per-recommendation provenance so T69 regression tests can measure recall.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T57.md:44:5. Implement `impact_from_diff` in `workflow_v2/impact_from_diff.rs`: accept a diff or list of changed files/symbols, walk dependent edges (`calls`, `imports`, `implements`, `extends`, `type_ref`, `depends_on`) up to a bounded depth (spec §Non-Negotiable Product Properties forbids unbounded traversal on hot paths), attach affected tests via `tested_by`, attach affected docs via `documents`, and surface high-impact warnings as `RiskNote`s.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T57.md:74:- Doc citation: cite spec headings `## Phase 8: Workflow Engine V2`, `## MCP Surface`, and `## Non-Negotiable Product Properties` in module doc comments.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T83.md:1:# T83 — Phase 11 — Partial-index handling + workspace-boundary tests
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T83.md:7:**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 11: Hardening](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-11-hardening), [§Non-Negotiable Product Properties](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#non-negotiable-product-properties), [§Scope Leakage](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#scope-leakage)
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T83.md:12:This task delivers two test modules that enforce two of the spec's hardest invariants: partial indexes must degrade gracefully (no panics, no silent dropped results), and workspace boundaries must hold (no silent broad workspace reads bypassing ignore rules; no cross-workspace memory leakage). Spec §Non-Negotiable Product Properties states "no silent broad workspace reads that bypass ignore rules or workspace boundaries"; spec §Scope Leakage names "user/org/branch memories leak into wrong workspaces" as a risk whose control is "scope-aware queries, enforced filters in store APIs, and negative tests." This task provides those negative tests.
