docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T84.md:7:**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 11: Hardening](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-11-hardening), [§Phase 3: Memory Graph Storage](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-3-memory-graph-storage), [§Fork Strategy](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#fork-strategy), [§MCP Tool Contract Principles](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#mcp-tool-contract-principles)
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T84.md:12:This task delivers two test modules that enforce the two long-term-compatibility surfaces of the fork: the storage migration path from the legacy Lattice schemas (Phase 3 memory rows, identity model, event-absent state) into the new schemas, and the MCP schema compatibility regression that confirms every backward-compat shim from R64 still functions. Spec §Phase 3 deliverables include "migration/import path from existing Lattice memory rows"; spec §Phase 11 deliverables list "migration tests" and "MCP schema compatibility tests" separately. Without these tests, an operator upgrading an existing Lattice deployment could silently lose memory or break a pinned assistant client.
