docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T69.md:7:**Spec anchor:** [§Measurable Success Criteria](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#measurable-success-criteria)
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T69.md:12:This task ships the regression tests that prove the cognitive workspace fork beats the baselines on every initial target from spec §Measurable Success Criteria. The tests run the redesigned tools (T56/T57) against the T66 fixture repos, feed the captured events into the T65 metrics collector, render the T68 regression report, and assert each spec §Measurable Success Criteria target. Without this task, the metrics infrastructure exists but no automated gate proves the system meets its stated goals — the Phase 9 DoD ("changes to retrieval, memory, and workflow behavior can be evaluated without relying on anecdote") would not be satisfied.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T69.md:16:> "Initial targets: 30 percent fewer discovery tool calls on benchmark tasks; 40 percent fewer irrelevant file reads; 80 percent memory inclusion precision on curated memory benchmarks; zero trusted display of known contradicted memory; zero trusted display of known stale memory without stale label; 90 percent correct relevant-test recommendation on curated tasks." (spec §Measurable Success Criteria)
