docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T45.md:12:This task makes every consolidation job — synchronous, background, manual-review, and LLM-driven — replay-safe and reversible. Spec §Non-Negotiable Product Properties demands "every background consolidation pass is recoverable, replayable, and observable" and spec §Consolidation Engine names `replay mode for rebuilding memory state from the event log` as one of the four consolidation modes. This task adds the replay driver, ensures that every applied proposal preserves prior state so reversal is mechanical, and verifies that replaying the event log reconstructs the same memory state without depending on wall-clock time, RNG order, or driver responses cached from the first run.
