 — final readiness review. Required headings:\n  - `## Spec coverage matrix` — one row per spec §Phase, status PASS/PASS-WITH-CAVEATS/BLOCK.\n  - `## Measurable success criteria` — one row per target from spec §Measurable Success Criteria (initial targets); evidence file path.\n  - `## Risk controls in place` — one row per risk from spec §Risks; control implementation evidence.\n  - `## Ship verdict` — PASS or BLOCK.\n\nR89 verification includes a full `cargo test --workspace` + extension compile/lint/test.\n\nRead the spec yourself for exact text. Quote it. Read ui-specification.md and definition-of-done-checklist.md sections relevant to the tasks you write.\n\nFor each task: 5-10 concrete steps, exact file paths from tasks.json, exact verification commands from tasks.json.\n\nWrite all 19 files, then report file count + first 3 paths confirmed. Do NOT modify tasks.json, context.md, or plan.md. Do NOT implement any code in daemon/ or extension/.","agentId":"a78780aeb6875bd27","agentType":"general-purpose","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 19 task brief files written successfully.\n\n**File count:** 19 (T71, T72, T73, T74, T75, T76, T77, R78, R79, T80, T81, T82, T83, T84, T85, T86, R87, R88, R89).\n\n**First 3 paths confirmed:**\n- `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T71.md`\n- `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T72.md`\n- `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T73.md`\n\n**Summary of coverage:**\n- **T71–T76** (frontend): each task brief follows the prior-agent template (Goal, Spec excerpts, Inputs, Steps, Files expected, Verification, Coding-standard checks with UI-specification subsection, Definition of done). Every frontend brief honors the mandated UI-spec subsection covering i18n via `i18n.t(...)`, native `<dialog>` modals (no `window.confirm/prompt/alert`), `try/catch` with `vscode.window.showErrorMessage(err.message)` (the VS Code analogue to `parseApiError + toast.error`), `vscode.window.showQuickPick` for ID inputs, sortable headers / pagination, and loading/empty/error/badge states for every interactive surface.\n- **T77** (extension UI smoke tests): VS Code test runner via `node ./out/test/runTest.js`; covers activation, view registration, and per-subview render under happy/empty/error.\n- **R78** (Phase 10 frontend review): all required headings (Spec alignment, Coding-standard alignment, UI-specification compliance walking ui-specification.md sections explicitly, i18n coverage, Findings, Verdict).\n- **R79** (Extension↔Daemon contract gate): introduces `extension/src/test/contract.test.ts`; required headings (Contract surfaces, Round-trip evidence, Schema surfaces, Findings, Verdict).\n- **T80–T84** (Phase 11 hardening tests): large-repo perf (with P99 budgets from Phases 1+2), concurrency (parallel sessions / write contention / replay-safe), recovery + corruption, partial-index + workspace-boundary (per spec §Non-Negotiable Product Properties), migration + MCP schema compat regression (uses R64 shims).\n- **T85** (documentation suite): all eleven required docs from spec §Documentation Requirements.\n- **T86** (runbook + recovery playbook): quotes the `pkill -f lattice && cp daemon/target/release/lattice extension/bin/ && cp daemon/target/release/lattice ~/.vscode/extensions/lattice.lattice-0.1.0/bin/` sequence from `lattice/CLAUDE.md` and documents the replay-from-snapshot procedure validated by T82.\n- **R87** (Phase 11 hardening + docs review): required headings including Doc coverage matrix (one row per required doc from spec §Documentation Requirements) and Hardening evidence.\n- **R88** (Definition-of-Done gate): all nine checklist sections from `shared/templates/definition-of-done-checklist.md`; `## Explicit Deferrals` must be empty or list each deferral with reason+owner+target-date per the execution philosophy in `/home/pete/.claude/CLAUDE.md`.\n- **R89** (Final readiness review): required matrices (Spec coverage by phase, Measurable success criteria with evidence file paths, Risk controls in place with implementation+test evidence), plus a binding Ship verdict (PASS or BLOCK). Verification runs full `cargo test --workspace` and extension compile/lint/test.\n\nNo code in `daemon/` or `extension/` was modified. `tasks.json`, `context.md`, and `plan.md` were not modified."}],"totalDurationMs":987098,"totalTokens":160303,"totalToolUseCount":45,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":825,"cache_read_input_tokens":158112,"output_tokens":1365,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":825},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1365,"cache_read_input_tokens":158112,"cache_creation_input_tokens":825,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":825,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":15,"searchCount":2,"bashCount":9,"editFileCount":19,"linesAdded":1605,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T74.log:4051:docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T71.log:7950:docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T37.log:2061:docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T04.log:2717:./docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/00-decompose.log:651:{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_013ZXuTanJH7X6D7LHKK4aiQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RsNa6ebsnWVeUhpsNvGQen","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T06.md","content":"# T06 — Phase 1 — Identity type system (File, Symbol, Doc, Section, Event, Memory, Handle)\n\n**Phase:** 1\n**Type:** backend\n**Model class:** advanced\n**Depends on:** R05\n**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 1: Unified Identity Model](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-1-unified-identity-model)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task introduces the unified identity type system that every later substrate (event log, memory graph, working memory, retrieval, verification) depends on. Spec §Phase 1 states \"Identity must precede the event log. An event that references a file, symbol, or doc by unstable name cannot be reliably replayed or used for consolidation.\" The task delivers stable, encodable, decodable, hashable id types for each of the seven identity kinds plus the encoding/decoding rules that make them compact in MCP payloads. The existing `SymbolId { file, name, byte_offset }` is generalized into a common identity model.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Phase 1 Deliverables: stable ids for files, symbols, docs, sections, events, memories, and context handles; identity resolver for paths, symbols, headings, tests, and event refs; explicit identity serialization in MCP payloads; compatibility support for legacy name-based references; tests for duplicate symbol names, renamed files, moved sections, and branch changes.\"\n\n> \"Definition of done: every workflow output can be expanded through a stable identity; ambiguous names return ambiguity diagnostics instead of arbitrary matches; identity resolution adds no more than 2ms P99 to hot-path tool calls.\"\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs: R05 review (validates Phase 0 artifacts) and the layout decisions in `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md` (decides whether identity is a `lattice-identity` crate or a `lattice-core::identity` module).\n- Existing files in the repo this task builds on:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/graph/` (current node identifier types)\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/intelligence/` (current `SymbolId` usage in `expand_context`)\n  - `docs/architecture/2026-04-11-stable-follow-up-handles.md` (existing handle conventions to honor and generalize)\n- Standards files to honor: `coding.md` hard limits (file ≤800 lines, function ≤50, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10), naming (intent over mechanism), single source of truth (replace ad-hoc id strings, do not fork them); `AGENTS.md` backward-compatibility (legacy `SymbolId` callers must keep compiling via a re-export or `From` impl).\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read the crate boundary plan from T03 to confirm whether identity lives in `daemon/crates/lattice-identity/` or `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/`. The files_expected list assumes the in-`lattice-core` module layout; if T03 chose a separate crate, mirror the file structure under that crate and update the workspace `Cargo.toml`.\n2. Create `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/mod.rs` declaring the `kinds`, `encoding`, and `tests` submodules and re-exporting the public identity types.\n3. In `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/kinds.rs`, define one struct per identity kind with the exact fields required by the spec node/event/memory model:\n   - `FileId { workspace_id, repo_relative_path, content_hash }`\n   - `SymbolId { file: FileId, qualified_name, byte_offset, kind }` (generalizing the existing `SymbolId`)\n   - `DocId { workspace_id, repo_relative_path, content_hash }`\n   - `SectionId { doc: DocId, heading_path: Vec<String>, byte_offset }`\n   - `EventId { workspace_id, ulid }` (ULID for monotonic ordering)\n   - `MemoryId { workspace_id, ulid }`\n   - `ContextHandleId { workspace_id, session_id, ulid }`\n4. Each id type derives `Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Hash, serde::Serialize, serde::Deserialize`. Implement `Display` to produce the compact MCP wire form.\n5. Define a common `IdentityKind` enum and an `Identity` enum that wraps the seven kinds so any subsystem can hold a heterogeneous identity reference.\n6. In `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/encoding.rs`, implement compact wire encoding rules: a stable string form (`file:<workspace>/<path>@<hash>`, `symbol:<file>#<qname>@<offset>`, `event:<workspace>/<ulid>`, etc.) and a decoder that round-trips. Reject malformed strings with a typed `IdentityDecodeError`.\n7. Provide `From<old_SymbolId> for SymbolId` and a re-export under the prior path so existing callers continue compiling.\n8. In `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/tests.rs`, write unit tests for: round-trip encoding for every kind; equality semantics; hash stability across process restarts (deterministic for same inputs); `IdentityDecodeError` cases (empty, missing prefix, malformed hash); `From<old_SymbolId>` migration.\n9. Add the module to `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/lib.rs` with `pub mod identity;` and document the substrate in a module-level doc comment that cites the spec heading.\n10. Run `cd daemon && cargo build -p lattice-core` and `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib identity::tests` to confirm green.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/mod.rs` — module entrypoint, re-exports, module docs citing spec §Phase 1.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/kinds.rs` — the seven id structs, `Identity` enum, `IdentityKind` enum.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/encoding.rs` — compact wire form encode/decode with `IdentityDecodeError`.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/tests.rs` — unit tests covering round-trip, equality, hashing, decode errors, and the legacy `SymbolId` migration shim.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/mod.rs` — confirms the module file exists.\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/kinds.rs` — confirms the kinds file exists.\n- `cd daemon && cargo build -p lattice-core` — confirms the crate compiles with the new module integrated.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib identity::tests` — confirms all identity unit tests pass.\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines (verify with `wc -l daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/*.rs`).\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10 — applies to every encode/decode helper.\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code.\n- No unjustified `// allow(...)` or suppressions; if `#[allow(clippy::...)]` is required, justify on the same line.\n- Public API names follow intent-over-mechanism naming (`FileId`, `SymbolId`, `IdentityDecodeError`).\n- For schema changes: not applicable (no SQL schema in this task); type-level schema parity is asserted via the `Identity` enum covering all seven kinds with no orphan fields.\n- Doc citation: cite the exact `## Phase 1: Unified Identity Model` heading from the spec in `mod.rs`; reference `docs/architecture/2026-04-11-stable-follow-up-handles.md` headings rather than duplicating prior handle behavior (per `lattice/CLAUDE.md` § Markdown Heading References).\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs).\n- [ ] Every verification command in tasks.json passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: no item from spec §Phase 1 punted to a later phase.\n- [ ] If a backward-incompatible change was needed, the AGENTS.md \"Backward-compatibility and contract discipline\" section was followed and the architecture doc was updated in the same task.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":615,"cache_read_input_tokens":49571,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":615,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_016juPk15H1M5x3FpzubRVsP","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"36cefa05-6830-4681-aa11-def156e8cd29","request_id":"req_011Cb7Mcwaxi2NndD8b7oC78","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 0+1 task briefs"}
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T74.log:4052:docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T71.log:7951:docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T37.log:2062:docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T04.log:2718:./docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/00-decompose.log:660:{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_013ZXuTanJH7X6D7LHKK4aiQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VyFsJMQCiudocXkZ3sZYhd","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T07.md","content":"# T07 — Phase 1 — Identity resolver with ambiguity diagnostics\n\n**Phase:** 1\n**Type:** backend\n**Model class:** balanced\n**Depends on:** T06\n**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 1: Unified Identity Model](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-1-unified-identity-model)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task implements the resolver that turns user-supplied or LLM-supplied references — paths, qualified symbol names, doc headings, test names, event refs — into the stable `Identity` values defined in T06. Spec §Phase 1 names \"identity resolver for paths, symbols, headings, tests, and event refs\" as a deliverable and binds the resolver to return ambiguity diagnostics rather than arbitrary matches when an input has multiple candidate identities. Without this resolver, every later phase would re-implement name→id lookups inconsistently, and ambiguity would be silently swallowed.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Phase 1 Deliverables: ... identity resolver for paths, symbols, headings, tests, and event refs ... compatibility support for legacy name-based references.\"\n\n> \"Definition of done: every workflow output can be expanded through a stable identity; ambiguous names return ambiguity diagnostics instead of arbitrary matches.\"\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs: identity types from T06 (`daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/kinds.rs`, `encoding.rs`).\n- Existing files in the repo this task builds on:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/graph/` (workspace graph that backs path/symbol lookups)\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/storage/` (SQLite-backed lookups for files, symbols, docs, sections)\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/parser/` (doc heading and symbol extraction the resolver consumes)\n- Standards files to honor: `coding.md` hard limits, naming (intent over mechanism), error handling (resolver errors must be structured, never silent); `AGENTS.md` (resolver public API is binding once shipped — any change is a contract change).\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Create `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/resolver.rs` with a `pub struct IdentityResolver` that holds references to the graph, storage, and parser indexes needed to answer lookups.\n2. Define the resolver public API:\n   - `resolve_path(&self, workspace: &WorkspaceId, path: &str) -> Result<FileId, ResolveError>`\n   - `resolve_symbol(&self, workspace: &WorkspaceId, qualified_name: &str) -> ResolveOutcome<SymbolId>`\n   - `resolve_section(&self, workspace: &WorkspaceId, doc: &DocId, heading: &str) -> ResolveOutcome<SectionId>`\n   - `resolve_test(&self, workspace: &WorkspaceId, test_name: &str) -> ResolveOutcome<SymbolId>` (tests are identified as symbols with a `Test` kind)\n   - `resolve_event_ref(&self, workspace: &WorkspaceId, ref_str: &str) -> Result<EventId, ResolveError>`\n3. Create `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/ambiguity.rs` with the `ResolveOutcome<T>` enum (`Unique(T)`, `Ambiguous(AmbiguityReport<T>)`, `NotFound(ResolveError)`) and the `AmbiguityReport<T>` struct carrying the list of candidates plus a `disambiguation_hint` describing how the caller can narrow the query (suggest adding parent module, file path, byte offset, etc.).\n4. The resolver must never pick arbitrarily when multiple matches exist — return `Ambiguous`. Tests in T09 will assert this on duplicate symbol names.\n5. Add a legacy compatibility helper `pub fn resolve_legacy_symbol_name(&self, name: &str) -> ResolveOutcome<SymbolId>` that takes a name without workspace context and routes to the resolver via the default workspace, preserving older MCP payloads.\n6. Implement caching: keep a small LRU keyed by `(workspace, query)` so the same resolution within a session does not re-traverse the graph. Cache hits must still preserve ambiguity semantics — a cached `Ambiguous` returns `Ambiguous`.\n7. Errors are structured: `ResolveError::WorkspaceNotIndexed`, `ResolveError::Malformed`, `ResolveError::IndexLagBehind { latest_event_id }`. No bare `String` errors.\n8. Add module-level docs in both files citing spec §Phase 1.\n9. Register the new submodules in `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/mod.rs` with `pub mod resolver;` and `pub mod ambiguity;`.\n10. Write smoke unit tests inline (the full ambiguity / rename / branch-change test matrix is owned by T09): construct a tiny resolver fixture and assert `resolve_path` returns a `FileId`, `resolve_symbol` on a duplicate name returns `Ambiguous`, and `resolve_legacy_symbol_name` falls back correctly.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/resolver.rs` — `IdentityResolver` struct, the five `resolve_*` methods, LRU cache, structured `ResolveError`.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/ambiguity.rs` — `ResolveOutcome<T>`, `AmbiguityReport<T>`, `disambiguation_hint` helpers.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/resolver.rs` — confirms the resolver file exists.\n- `cd daemon && cargo build -p lattice-core` — confirms the crate compiles with the resolver and ambiguity modules wired into `lattice-core`.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib identity::resolver` — confirms the resolver smoke tests pass.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib identity::ambiguity` — confirms the ambiguity module tests pass.\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines (verify with `wc -l daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/resolver.rs daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/ambiguity.rs`).\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10 — every `resolve_*` method must fit; extract candidate-collection helpers if needed.\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code.\n- No unjustified `// allow(...)` or suppressions.\n- Public API names follow intent-over-mechanism naming (`resolve_symbol` not `lookup`, `AmbiguityReport` not `MultiResult`).\n- For schema changes: not applicable (resolver consumes existing storage).\n- Doc citation: cite the exact `## Phase 1: Unified Identity Model` heading from the spec in module docs; if any non-obvious caching or LRU choice is made, cite the heading from `docs/architecture/2026-04-11-stable-follow-up-handles.md` that authorizes the behavior (per `lattice/CLAUDE.md` § Markdown Heading References).\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs).\n- [ ] Every verification command in tasks.json passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: no item from spec §Phase 1 punted to a later phase.\n- [ ] If a backward-incompatible change was needed, the AGENTS.md \"Backward-compatibility and contract discipline\" section was followed and the architecture doc was updated in the same task.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":615,"cache_read_input_tokens":49571,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":615,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_016juPk15H1M5x3FpzubRVsP","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"1a20f582-7bfb-4d3c-8dba-826aa42e26d0","request_id":"req_011Cb7Mcwaxi2NndD8b7oC78","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 0+1 task briefs"}
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T74.log:4053:docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T71.log:7952:docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T37.log:2065:docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T04.log:2721:./docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/00-decompose.log:672:{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_013ZXuTanJH7X6D7LHKK4aiQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016wpFR2N3dUb7fdjiDggmL3","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T08.md","content":"# T08 — Phase 1 — Identity serialization in MCP payloads + legacy name compatibility shim\n\n**Phase:** 1\n**Type:** backend\n**Model class:** balanced\n**Depends on:** T07\n**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 1: Unified Identity Model](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-1-unified-identity-model)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task wires the new `Identity` types into the MCP JSON-RPC surface so every workflow tool response carries stable identities the client can expand later, while preserving legacy name-based fields so existing clients continue to function. Spec §Phase 1 deliverables include \"explicit identity serialization in MCP payloads\" and \"compatibility support for legacy name-based references\". The compatibility shim is the binding mechanism by which T02's MCP compatibility policy is honored for Phase 1.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Phase 1 Deliverables: ... explicit identity serialization in MCP payloads; compatibility support for legacy name-based references.\"\n\n> \"Definition of done: every workflow output can be expanded through a stable identity.\"\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs:\n  - T06 identity types (`daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/kinds.rs`, `encoding.rs`).\n  - T07 resolver and ambiguity modules (`resolver.rs`, `ambiguity.rs`).\n  - T02 compatibility policy (`docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md`) — binding for which tools must add additive identity fields vs. shimmed legacy fields.\n- Existing files in the repo this task builds on:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` (current MCP dispatch and payload shapes)\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/server.rs` (JSON-RPC server)\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/context_cache.rs` (handle cache that must store new `ContextHandleId`)\n- Standards files to honor: `coding.md` (no broken windows, single source of truth, schema parity), `AGENTS.md` (binding compatibility shim — every legacy field stays populated for one phase cycle).\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Create `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/serialization.rs` with serde helpers that emit the compact wire form defined in T06 `encoding.rs` and accept either compact form or structured object form on deserialize.\n2. Define a `pub struct IdentityPayload` containing both the compact `id` string and a structured `fields` object, plus an optional `legacy_name` field for backward compatibility. Serialization round-trips through both forms.\n3. Add `pub fn serialize_outcome<T: Into<Identity>>(outcome: ResolveOutcome<T>) -> IdentityPayloadOrAmbiguity` that converts the resolver outcome to the wire shape, preserving `Ambiguous` as a structured diagnostic instead of an arbitrary pick.\n4. Create `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/identity_payload.rs` with the MCP wiring: a wrapper that decorates every workflow tool response (or its top-level pivot list) with `IdentityPayload` values and preserves the legacy name field listed in the T02 compatibility policy for each tool.\n5. Wire one representative tool (`get_context_capsule` or `prepare_change`) end-to-end through the new serialization wrapper as a proof of integration; full Phase 8 redesign of every tool is owned later, but Phase 1 must demonstrate the integration path works without regressing existing clients.\n6. Add tests under `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/serialization.rs` (`#[cfg(test)] mod tests`) covering: compact-form round-trip, structured-form acceptance, legacy-name preservation, ambiguity payload shape.\n7. Add tests under `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/identity_payload.rs` covering: a full tool response that includes both identity payloads and legacy fields, and a response where the resolver returned `Ambiguous` (the response must surface the ambiguity diagnostic rather than silently picking).\n8. Update the workflow tool that was wired in step 5 to emit identity payloads alongside its prior fields; document the change in `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md` under the per-tool classification.\n9. Run `cd daemon && cargo build --release`, `cd daemon && cargo test --workspace -- identity::serialization`, and `cd daemon && cargo test --workspace -- rpc::identity_payload` to confirm green.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/serialization.rs` — `IdentityPayload`, serde helpers, `serialize_outcome`, inline tests.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/identity_payload.rs` — MCP wrapper that decorates workflow responses with identity payloads and preserves legacy name fields.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/serialization.rs` — confirms the serialization module exists.\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/identity_payload.rs` — confirms the RPC integration module exists.\n- `cd daemon && cargo build --release` — confirms the full workspace builds in release profile with the new modules wired in.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test --workspace -- identity::serialization` — confirms the serialization tests pass.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test --workspace -- rpc::identity_payload` — confirms the RPC integration tests pass.\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines (verify with `wc -l daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/serialization.rs daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/identity_payload.rs`).\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10 — applies to every serde helper and wrapper.\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code.\n- No unjustified `// allow(...)` or suppressions.\n- Public API names follow intent-over-mechanism naming (`IdentityPayload`, `serialize_outcome`, not `IdData` or `to_json`).\n- For schema changes: not applicable (no SQL schema added); JSON schema parity is asserted by tests covering both legacy and new fields.\n- Doc citation: cite the exact `## Phase 1: Unified Identity Model` heading from the spec and the per-tool classification heading from `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md` for every additive field introduced (per `lattice/CLAUDE.md` § Markdown Heading References).\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs).\n- [ ] Every verification command in tasks.json passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: no item from spec §Phase 1 punted to a later phase.\n- [ ] If a backward-incompatible change was needed, the AGENTS.md \"Backward-compatibility and contract discipline\" section was followed and the architecture doc was updated in the same task.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":615,"cache_read_input_tokens":49571,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":615,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_016juPk15H1M5x3FpzubRVsP","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"f2172cba-383d-413f-b510-a7ed9826dfd5","request_id":"req_011Cb7Mcwaxi2NndD8b7oC78","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 0+1 task briefs"}
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T74.log:4060:docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T71.log:7959:docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T37.log:2083:docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T04.log:2739:./docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/00-decompose.log:797:{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_019ScAFhwj15KgrT4jB8Uvi8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DeEj2PHYWT2tYJ3BkufH5S","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/R79.md","content":"# R79 — Contract gate — Extension ↔ Daemon review-UI MCP plumbing\n\n**Phase:** Contract gate after Phase 10\n**Type:** review\n**Model class:** advanced\n**Depends on:** R64, R78\n**Spec anchor:** [§9. MCP Surface](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#9-mcp-surface), [§10. Human Review Surface](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#10-human-review-surface), [§MCP Tool Contract Principles](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#mcp-tool-contract-principles)\n**Standards reviewed:** Cadres coding standard (`/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md`); Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Purpose\n\nThis review is the contract gate between the Phase 10 review UI and the daemon MCP surface that powers it. Every method on `ReviewRpcBridge` calls a tool registered on the daemon side; this gate verifies that every method has a matching tool, that the JSON shapes round-trip end to end, that the schema is documented and regression-tested, and that no surface added by Phases 6–9 was forgotten on the extension side. The gate exists because UI compile + lint cannot detect contract drift — only an integration test that sends a real request to a real daemon and asserts the response shape can. Spec §Non-Negotiable Product Properties demands \"every public MCP contract is documented and regression-tested\"; this review enforces that for the review UI surface.\n\n## Inputs to read\n\n- Every artifact produced by T71–T77 (extension review surface).\n- Every artifact produced by Phase 6–9 MCP work the review UI depends on, including the R64 contract gate output for the MCP tool schema.\n- Existing files this review cross-checks:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` — registered MCP tools.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/server.rs` — JSON-RPC server.\n  - `extension/src/review/rpcBridge.ts` — typed extension-side bridge.\n  - `extension/src/daemon.ts` — underlying JSON-RPC client.\n  - `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md` (from T02) — backward-compatibility policy this gate enforces.\n- Spec sections: `## 9. MCP Surface`, `## 10. Human Review Surface`, `## MCP Tool Contract Principles`.\n- Shared standards: `/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md` (schema parity, single source of truth); `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/AGENTS.md` (backward-compatibility discipline).\n\n## Review procedure\n\n1. Enumerate every method exposed by `ReviewRpcBridge` and confirm each maps to a registered MCP tool in `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs`. Any orphan method on either side is a blocker.\n2. For every mapped pair, inspect the typed request and response shapes on the TypeScript side (`rpcBridge.ts`) and the corresponding Rust schema in `mcp.rs` (and its serde structs). Field-by-field comparison: type, required/optional, name. Drift is a blocker per `coding.md` §Schema parity.\n3. Cross-check `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md` (T02) — every review-UI tool is either `stable`, `additive`, or `redesigned-with-shim`; nothing is undocumented.\n4. Create `extension/src/test/contract.test.ts` (this is the deliverable contract test). The test launches a real daemon process via the existing pattern in `extension/src/test/`, sends one round-trip request per review-UI bridge method, and asserts the response parses into the typed shape. Include happy-path requests and an error-path request per tool. Tests use the real daemon binary (`daemon/target/release/lattice`), not a mock.\n5. Run the contract suite with `cd extension && npm install && npm run compile && npm test`. Confirm every round-trip passes. If the daemon binary is not present in `extension/bin/`, the test setup builds and copies per `lattice/CLAUDE.md` Build/Deploy: `cd daemon && cargo build --release && cp daemon/target/release/lattice extension/bin/`.\n6. Confirm the contract test exercises every review-UI tool from `rpcBridge.ts`: memory listing, evidence inspection, promotion queue read + apply + reject, contradiction queue read + apply + reject, stale listing, verify_memory, event trace read, retrieval explanation read, consolidation queue read + retry, indexing health read, graph health read + recompute.\n7. Grep `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` for the corresponding tool registrations and confirm each accepts the documented request shape and returns the documented response shape.\n8. Cross-check that backward-compat shims from R64 (if any) are still in place: every legacy tool name continues to route to the new implementation.\n\n## Required sections in the review output file\n\nThe reviewer writes to `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R79-contract-extension-daemon.md` with these mandatory headings (each must contain real findings, not \"n/a\"):\n\n- `## Contract surfaces` — table of every `ReviewRpcBridge` method, the corresponding daemon tool name, the request shape, the response shape, and the spec citation. One row per method.\n- `## Round-trip evidence` — for every method, the contract-test name in `extension/src/test/contract.test.ts` that exercises it; the test output snippet showing the request, the response, and the assertion that the typed shape parsed; the daemon log line showing the request was received.\n- `## Schema surfaces` — TypeScript ↔ Rust field comparison table per tool. Columns: TS field, TS type, TS required, Rust field, Rust type, Rust required, parity verdict. Any drift is flagged.\n- `## Findings` — issues found, severity (`blocker`, `major`, `minor`), suggested follow-up tasks. Follow-up tasks must be opened in this build (do not defer outside).\n- `## Verdict` — `PASS`, `PASS-WITH-FOLLOWUP-TASK-Txx`, or `BLOCK` (with named blockers).\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R79-contract-extension-daemon.md` — confirms the review markdown exists where downstream tasks can read it.\n- `test -f extension/src/test/contract.test.ts` — confirms the new contract test file exists.\n- `grep -q '## Contract surfaces' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R79-contract-extension-daemon.md` — confirms contract surfaces enumerated under a dedicated heading.\n- `grep -q '## Round-trip evidence' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R79-contract-extension-daemon.md` — confirms round-trip evidence is present.\n- `cd extension && npm run compile` — TypeScript compile (including the new contract test) succeeds.\n- `cd extension && npm test` — the contract suite plus all prior tests pass against a real daemon.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Review markdown file exists at the path verification commands check.\n- [ ] `extension/src/test/contract.test.ts` exists, compiles, and passes against the real daemon binary.\n- [ ] Every required section above is present with concrete content (not \"n/a\").\n- [ ] `## Schema surfaces` and `## Findings` are also present (not gated by tasks.json verification but required for completeness).\n- [ ] If verdict is BLOCK, the blocking issues are listed and a follow-up task is opened in this build (never deferred to a future session per `/home/pete/.claude/CLAUDE.md` execution philosophy).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":101320,"cache_read_input_tokens":10845,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":101320,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XjrTa6YAS1dmMW989ZPauZ","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"ce6e8520-9b5f-42b8-a09b-8be0a2ce22df","request_id":"req_011Cb7NGicAyFMeCwEAwKwU2","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 10+11+Final task briefs"}
