docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T51.md:12:This task ships two spec-required Phase 7 mechanisms. First, time-bound expiry: memories with an `expires_at` reach the `expired` state automatically when their timestamp passes, and the verifier emits the corresponding `MarkExpired` proposal. Second, incremental verification: the verifier walks only memories whose evidence cites files/symbols that actually changed since the last graph snapshot, never a full rescan. The spec is explicit that "large repos cannot tolerate full rescans for every memory" — this is the mechanism that makes Phase 7 scalable.
