docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T-followup-R05-A.md:12:R05 finding F1. The `find_relevant_tests` benchmark in `daemon/crates/lattice-core/benches/baseline_workflows.rs:309-318` invokes the workflow against `src/auth.ts` + `src/session.ts` and symbols `loginUser` + `createSession`. The fixture also materializes `tests/auth.test.ts` and `tests/session.test.ts` (`fixture_files()` at lines 180–195). Despite that, the regenerated `baselines/baseline_metrics.json` records `"candidate_count": 0` for `find_relevant_tests`. The latency baseline is still valid as an empty-result baseline, but the workflow does not exercise the tested-by graph traversal path.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T-followup-R05-A.md:22:1. Register the fixture test files through the same indexer path that production uses so `find_relevant_tests` sees them as test candidates. Investigate why the existing fixture tests are not picked up — likely a missing tested-by edge or a missing test-discovery rule for the fixture workspace layout.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T-followup-R05-A.md:25:Whichever path is taken, the bench fixture must still be deterministic (no network, no external repo) and the regenerated `baseline_metrics.json` must show `"candidate_count": >= 1` for `find_relevant_tests`.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T-followup-R05-A.md:35:- [ ] Bench fixture remains deterministic and self-contained.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T69.md:6:**Depends on:** T65, T66, T67, T68
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T69.md:12:This task ships the regression tests that prove the cognitive workspace fork beats the baselines on every initial target from spec §Measurable Success Criteria. The tests run the redesigned tools (T56/T57) against the T66 fixture repos, feed the captured events into the T65 metrics collector, render the T68 regression report, and assert each spec §Measurable Success Criteria target. Without this task, the metrics infrastructure exists but no automated gate proves the system meets its stated goals — the Phase 9 DoD ("changes to retrieval, memory, and workflow behavior can be evaluated without relying on anecdote") would not be satisfied.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T69.md:26:  - T66 — fixture repos + `golden_anchors.json` + `cognitive_workspace_benchmark`.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T69.md:38:2. Implement `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/metrics/regression_tests.rs` containing one `#[test]` per spec §Measurable Success Criteria initial target. Each test loads the T66 fixtures, runs the redesigned tools end-to-end against the golden tasks, feeds events into the T65 `MetricsCollector`, and asserts the corresponding threshold using the T68 `SuccessCriteriaThresholds`:
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T69.md:41:   - `test_memory_inclusion_precision_at_least_80pct` — `MemoryInclusionPrecision` ≥ 0.80 on the curated memory benchmark tasks from T66.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T69.md:42:   - `test_zero_trusted_display_of_contradicted_memory` — `ContradictionMissedRate` equals 0 across all fixture tasks.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T69.md:43:   - `test_zero_trusted_display_of_stale_memory_without_label` — `StaleMemorySurfacedRate` equals 0 across all fixture tasks (stale memories may appear, but never without an explicit stale label per spec §Phase 7 DoD).
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T69.md:44:   - `test_relevant_test_recommendation_at_least_90pct` — `TestsRecommendedVsNeeded` recall ≥ 0.90 on the curated tasks from T66.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T69.md:47:5. Implement a helper `MetricsTestHarness` in the same file (or a sibling `regression_harness.rs`) that loads fixtures deterministically, executes a fixed tool sequence per task, captures events into an isolated `.lattice/events.db`, and returns the resulting `MetricValue`s. The harness encapsulates the deterministic-seed and fixture-freeze policy from T66 so per-test code is short.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T69.md:53:- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/metrics/regression_tests.rs` — one `#[test]` per spec §Measurable Success Criteria initial target asserting the redesigned system beats baselines (30% discovery, 40% irrelevant reads, 80% memory precision, 0 stale/contradicted trusted display, 90% test recommendation); shared `MetricsTestHarness` for deterministic fixture execution; per-failure diagnostics via T68 evidence pointers.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T69.md:58:- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib metrics::regression_tests -- --include-ignored` — every spec §Measurable Success Criteria regression test passes against the T66 fixture repos.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T69.md:65:- No silent error handling — every fixture load / harness failure produces a typed error; no test uses `unwrap()` on a `Result` that could legitimately fail without diagnostic.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T69.md:67:- Public API names follow intent-over-mechanism naming (`MetricsTestHarness::run_fixture_task`, not `MetricsTestHarness::go`).
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T41.md:43:9. In `consolidation/deterministic_tests.rs`, write per-scanner tests on a seeded memory fixture: (a) two near-duplicate memories produce a supersession proposal, (b) a memory whose anchor file was deleted produces a `MarkStale` proposal, (c) a never-accessed low-score memory produces a `Demote` proposal, (d) a memory whose evidence still matches produces a `Refresh` proposal, (e) every scanner is a no-op (zero proposals) on a fresh empty store, (f) every proposal carries `prior_state` and `proposed_state` and routes through the T39 runtime (assert no direct `memory.store.write(...)` calls — verify via a test seam that counts direct writes).
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T41.md:50:- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/deterministic_tests.rs` — per-scanner fixtures, proposal-routing assertions, no-silent-write guard.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T45.md:43:8. In `consolidation/replay_tests.rs`, write tests that: (a) `replay(FromGenesis)` on a fixture with 50 mixed deterministic + LLM proposals reconstructs the same memory state byte-for-byte (state hash match), (b) reversal of a `Refresh` proposal restores `last_verified_at` exactly, (c) reversal of a `Supersede` proposal flips status back and clears the `memory_links` edge, (d) replay with no LLM driver available succeeds when provenance cache is populated and fails cleanly when it is not, (e) replay never calls the live `LlmDriver` (assert via a fake driver whose `complete` panics — replay must never invoke it), (f) reversal is idempotent: reverting an already-reverted proposal is a typed `AlreadyReverted` outcome, not a panic.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/results/R64.md:6:- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp_schema_tests.rs` — schema regression test entry point and shared fixture (`SchemaFixture`).
