n: corrupted event payloads, partial snapshots, replay-from-snapshot.\n- T83 — partial-index handling + workspace-boundary tests (per spec §Non-Negotiable Product Properties \"no silent broad workspace reads\").\n- T84 — migration tests + MCP schema compatibility regression (covers backward-compat shims from R64).\n- T85 — documentation suite. Required docs from spec §Documentation Requirements:\n  - successor architecture overview\n  - MCP contract reference (was T61)\n  - memory model reference\n  - event log design\n  - consolidation design\n  - retrieval/ranking design\n  - verification/freshness design\n  - operator guide\n  - migration guide from Lattice\n  - benchmark/evaluation guide\n  - extension review UI guide\n- T86 — operator runbook + recovery playbook. Includes deploy sequence: `pkill -f lattice && cp daemon/target/release/lattice extension/bin/ && cp daemon/target/release/lattice ~/.vscode/extensions/lattice.lattice-0.1.0/bin/` from `lattice/CLAUDE.md` Build/Deploy. Includes replay-from-snapshot procedure.\n- R87 — Phase 11 review. Required headings: `## Spec alignment`, `## Coding-standard alignment`, `## Doc coverage matrix` (one row per required doc from spec §Documentation Requirements), `## Hardening evidence`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict`.\n- R88 — definition-of-done gate. Required headings (one per checklist section from `shared/templates/definition-of-done-checklist.md`):\n  - `## Workflow Completion`\n  - `## Failure Handling`\n  - `## Security, Tenancy, and Audit`\n  - `## Data Integrity and Workflow Controls`\n  - `## Observability and Recovery`\n  - `## Performance and Scale`\n  - `## Documentation and Operator Readiness`\n  - `## Verification Evidence`\n  - `## Explicit Deferrals` — this MUST be either empty (no deferrals) or list each deferral with reason + owner + target date per the execution philosophy in `/home/pete/.claude/CLAUDE.md`. No silent deferrals.\n- R89 — final readiness review. Required headings:\n  - `## Spec coverage matrix` — one row per spec §Phase, status PASS/PASS-WITH-CAVEATS/BLOCK.\n  - `## Measurable success criteria` — one row per target from spec §Measurable Success Criteria (initial targets); evidence file path.\n  - `## Risk controls in place` — one row per risk from spec §Risks; control implementation evidence.\n  - `## Ship verdict` — PASS or BLOCK.\n\nR89 verification includes a full `cargo test --workspace` + extension compile/lint/test.\n\nRead the spec yourself for exact text. Quote it. Read ui-specification.md and definition-of-done-checklist.md sections relevant to the tasks you write.\n\nFor each task: 5-10 concrete steps, exact file paths from tasks.json, exact verification commands from tasks.json.\n\nWrite all 19 files, then report file count + first 3 paths confirmed. Do NOT modify tasks.json, context.md, or plan.md. Do NOT implement any code in daemon/ or extension/.","agentId":"a78780aeb6875bd27","agentType":"general-purpose","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 19 task brief files written successfully.\n\n**File count:** 19 (T71, T72, T73, T74, T75, T76, T77, R78, R79, T80, T81, T82, T83, T84, T85, T86, R87, R88, R89).\n\n**First 3 paths confirmed:**\n- `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T71.md`\n- `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T72.md`\n- `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T73.md`\n\n**Summary of coverage:**\n- **T71–T76** (frontend): each task brief follows the prior-agent template (Goal, Spec excerpts, Inputs, Steps, Files expected, Verification, Coding-standard checks with UI-specification subsection, Definition of done). Every frontend brief honors the mandated UI-spec subsection covering i18n via `i18n.t(...)`, native `<dialog>` modals (no `window.confirm/prompt/alert`), `try/catch` with `vscode.window.showErrorMessage(err.message)` (the VS Code analogue to `parseApiError + toast.error`), `vsc