 — final readiness review. Required headings:\n  - `## Spec coverage matrix` — one row per spec §Phase, status PASS/PASS-WITH-CAVEATS/BLOCK.\n  - `## Measurable success criteria` — one row per target from spec §Measurable Success Criteria (initial targets); evidence file path.\n  - `## Risk controls in place` — one row per risk from spec §Risks; control implementation evidence.\n  - `## Ship verdict` — PASS or BLOCK.\n\nR89 verification includes a full `cargo test --workspace` + extension compile/lint/test.\n\nRead the spec yourself for exact text. Quote it. Read ui-specification.md and definition-of-done-checklist.md sections relevant to the tasks you write.\n\nFor each task: 5-10 concrete steps, exact file paths from tasks.json, exact verification commands from tasks.json.\n\nWrite all 19 files, then report file count + first 3 paths confirmed. Do NOT modify tasks.json, context.md, or plan.md. Do NOT implement any code in daemon/ or extension/.","agentId":"a78780aeb6875bd27","agentType":"general-purpose","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 19 task brief files written successfully.\n\n**File count:** 19 (T71, T72, T73, T74, T75, T76, T77, R78, R79, T80, T81, T82, T83, T84, T85, T86, R87, R88, R89).\n\n**First 3 paths confirmed:**\n- `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T71.md`\n- `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T72.md`\n- `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T73.md`\n\n**Summary of coverage:**\n- **T71–T76** (frontend): each task brief follows the prior-agent template (Goal, Spec excerpts, Inputs, Steps, Files expected, Verification, Coding-standard checks with UI-specification subsection, Definition of done). Every frontend brief honors the mandated UI-spec subsection covering i18n via `i18n.t(...)`, native `<dialog>` modals (no `window.confirm/prompt/alert`), `try/catch` with `vscode.window.showErrorMessage(err.message)` (the VS Code analogue to `parseApiError + toast.error`), `vscode.window.showQuickPick` for ID inputs, sortable headers / pagination, and loading/empty/error/badge states for every interactive surface.\n- **T77** (extension UI smoke tests): VS Code test runner via `node ./out/test/runTest.js`; covers activation, view registration, and per-subview render under happy/empty/error.\n- **R78** (Phase 10 frontend review): all required headings (Spec alignment, Coding-standard alignment, UI-specification compliance walking ui-specification.md sections explicitly, i18n coverage, Findings, Verdict).\n- **R79** (Extension↔Daemon contract gate): introduces `extension/src/test/contract.test.ts`; required headings (Contract surfaces, Round-trip evidence, Schema surfaces, Findings, Verdict).\n- **T80–T84** (Phase 11 hardening tests): large-repo perf (with P99 budgets from Phases 1+2), concurrency (parallel sessions / write contention / replay-safe), recovery + corruption, partial-index + workspace-boundary (per spec §Non-Negotiable Product Properties), migration + MCP schema compat regression (uses R64 shims).\n- **T85** (documentation suite): all eleven required docs from spec §Documentation Requirements.\n- **T86** (runbook + recovery playbook): quotes the `pkill -f lattice && cp daemon/target/release/lattice extension/bin/ && cp daemon/target/release/lattice ~/.vscode/extensions/lattice.lattice-0.1.0/bin/` sequence from `lattice/CLAUDE.md` and documents the replay-from-snapshot procedure validated by T82.\n- **R87** (Phase 11 hardening + docs review): required headings including Doc coverage matrix (one row per required doc from spec §Documentation Requirements) and Hardening evidence.\n- **R88** (Definition-of-Done gate): all nine checklist sections from `shared/templates/definition-of-done-checklist.md`; `## Explicit Deferrals` must be empty or list each deferral with reason+owner+target-date per the execution philosophy in `/home/pete/.claude/CLAUDE.md`.\n- **R89** (Final readiness review): required matrices (Spec coverage by phase, Measurable success criteria with evidence file paths, Risk controls in place with implementation+test evidence), plus a binding Ship verdict (PASS or BLOCK). Verification runs full `cargo test --workspace` and extension compile/lint/test.\n\nNo code in `daemon/` or `extension/` was modified. `tasks.json`, `context.md`, and `plan.md` were not modified."}],"totalDurationMs":987098,"totalTokens":160303,"totalToolUseCount":45,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":825,"cache_read_input_tokens":158112,"output_tokens":1365,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":825},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1365,"cache_read_input_tokens":158112,"cache_creation_input_tokens":825,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":825,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":15,"searchCount":2,"bashCount":9,"editFileCount":19,"linesAdded":1605,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T74.log:4050:docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T71.log:7949:docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T37.log:2059:docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T04.log:2715:./docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/00-decompose.log:642:{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01XTcDiMrgdjkzP2h53pbga2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SUPWwtG9FxhbV4ptXmemxT","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T56.md","content":"# T56 — Phase 8 — Redesigned prepare_change + plan_edit + trace_scenario + diagnose_failure\n\n**Phase:** 8\n**Type:** backend\n**Model class:** advanced\n**Depends on:** R55\n**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 8: Workflow Engine V2](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-8-workflow-engine-v2)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task redesigns the four edit-planning workflow tools (`prepare_change`, `plan_edit`, `trace_scenario`, `diagnose_failure`) on top of the Phase 1–7 substrates: unified identity, event log, memory graph, retrieval pipeline, working memory, consolidation proposals, and verification status. The redesigned tools must compose those substrates in one call so that an assistant gets a complete edit-planning bundle (code anchors, docs, tests, memory with inclusion reasons, risks, verification commands) without first issuing dozens of low-level discovery calls. This is the central deliverable of Phase 8: spec §Phase 8 DoD requires \"common coding tasks require fewer manual discovery calls\" and \"workflows produce enough context to implement and verify changes without broad file dumping.\" Without this redesign, the new substrate work in Phases 1–7 stays invisible to callers.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Phase 8 Deliverables: redesigned versions of context, change planning, scenario tracing, failure diagnosis, docs retrieval, test selection, impact analysis, and playbook generation; workflow composition over graph, event, memory, and working-memory substrates; one-call edit-planning bundles with code, docs, tests, memory, risks, and verification commands; workflow outcome recording integrated by default.\"\n\n> \"Definition of done: common coding tasks require fewer manual discovery calls; workflows produce enough context to implement and verify changes without broad file dumping.\"\n\n> \"Every assistant-facing tool should return: overview, ranked pivots, relevant context, memory highlights, event episodes where relevant, suggested next expansion, stable handles, risks or uncertainty, compact/full render choice, structured payload.\" (spec §MCP Tool Contract Principles)\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs: R55 (Phase 7 verification engine review) — verification statuses (`verified` | `unverified` | `stale` | `contradicted` | `superseded` | `expired` | `invalidated`) must be surfaced inside the bundle so stale memory cannot appear as trusted guidance per spec §Phase 7 DoD.\n- Existing repo files this task builds on:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/intelligence/prepare_change.rs` — current `prepare_change` heuristics, retained as a compatibility shim per the T02 compatibility policy.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/intelligence/plan_edit.rs` — current patch-oriented planning.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/intelligence/trace_scenario.rs` — current scenario tracer.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/intelligence/diagnose_failure.rs` — current failure-diagnosis heuristics.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` — current MCP tool registration; new `workflow_v2` tools register alongside legacy names.\n  - Phase 1 identity types (`FileId`, `SymbolId`, `DocSectionId`, `EventId`, `MemoryId`, `ContextHandleId`).\n  - Phase 2 event writer (`EventWriter`) — every workflow call must emit `AssistantTaskStarted`, `ToolCalled`, `ContextBundleReturned`, `MemoryRetrieved`, and `PlanCreated` events.\n  - Phase 4 retrieval pipeline (intent classifier, anchor resolver, hybrid candidate retrieval, scoring with inclusion reasons).\n  - Phase 5 working-memory operations (`retrieve`, `summarize`, `filter`, `pin`, `evict`, `expand`, `compress`, `checkpoint`).\n  - Phase 7 verification engine (existence, span, scope, expiry checks).\n- Standards: Cadres coding standard §Hard limits (file ≤800 lines, function ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10), §Single source of truth, §No broken windows, §Schema parity, §Observability; Lattice rules on Markdown heading references for spec-bound behavior; `AGENTS.md` \"Backward-compatibility and contract discipline\" — legacy tool names continue to respond for a full phase cycle.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read spec §Phase 8 and §MCP Tool Contract Principles in full. Copy the bundle field list (\"overview, ranked pivots, relevant context, memory highlights, event episodes, suggested next expansion, stable handles, risks, render choice, structured payload\") into a doc comment on a shared `WorkflowBundle` struct so the schema is self-documenting.\n2. Create `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/mod.rs` exporting the four redesigned tools and the shared bundle types (`WorkflowBundle`, `Pivot`, `MemoryHighlight`, `EventEpisode`, `RiskNote`, `ExpansionHint`). Doc-comment the module with a reference to spec §Phase 8.\n3. Implement `prepare_change` in `workflow_v2/prepare_change.rs`: classify intent via the Phase 4 classifier, resolve anchors (paths, symbols, errors, APIs, config keys) into stable identities, run hybrid candidate retrieval across graph + docs + memory + events, apply the Phase 4 scorer, then assemble a `WorkflowBundle` containing code anchors, docs sections, candidate test files (from Phase 4 ranking + `tested_by` edges), memory highlights (each carrying inclusion reason + verification status per spec §MCP Tool Contract Principles), risk notes derived from contradiction/supersession state, and verification commands (`cargo test ...`, `npm test`, etc.) inferred from the affected build targets.\n4. Implement `plan_edit` in `workflow_v2/plan_edit.rs`: build on `prepare_change` output and produce a patch-oriented plan with ordered edit steps, each step referencing files/symbols by stable identity, named tests to add or run, docs sections to update (so spec §MCP Tool Contract Principles \"every workflow tool should record inputs, resolved anchors, selected candidates, excluded high-scoring candidates\" is satisfied).\n5. Implement `trace_scenario` in `workflow_v2/trace_scenario.rs`: walk call chains using the Phase 1 graph between anchor symbols, attaching event-episode evidence where the chain has been exercised before (from event log) and memory annotations describing prior successes/failures on that chain.\n6. Implement `diagnose_failure` in `workflow_v2/diagnose_failure.rs`: take a stack trace, compiler error, or failing test as input, extract anchors, query `FailurePattern` memories and prior `WorkflowFailed` events for similar signatures, surface likely culprit symbols with inclusion reasons + verification status, and suggest a candidate `prepare_change` follow-up bundle handle.\n7. Every tool must emit `AssistantTaskStarted`, `ToolCalled`, `ContextBundleReturned`, `MemoryRetrieved`, and `PlanCreated` events via the Phase 2 `EventWriter`. Hot-path budget per spec §Phase 2 DoD: event write must not add more than 5ms P99 on `prepare_change` / `get_context_capsule`.\n8. Every tool must produce compact rendering by default with stable expansion handles (per spec §MCP Tool Contract Principles \"compact rendering, full structured JSON, context handles, stable expansion targets, budget controls, diagnostic explanations where useful\"). The compact form must include enough inclusion reason for an assistant to trust the result.\n9. Register the four `workflow_v2` tools in `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` under their canonical names while keeping the legacy implementations registered with deprecation flags per the T02 compatibility policy.\n10. In `workflow_v2/edit_workflows_tests.rs`, write tests that: (a) round-trip each tool's request/response through serde; (b) assert that `prepare_change` returns a `WorkflowBundle` with at least one ranked pivot, one memory highlight (or an explicit empty rationale), one risk note, and at least one verification command for a fixture repo; (c) assert that no memory with `verification_status = stale | contradicted | superseded | expired | invalidated` appears without an explicit stale label (spec §Phase 7 DoD); (d) assert event-emission order and hot-path budget; (e) assert `plan_edit` produces ordered steps each referencing stable identity types; (f) assert `diagnose_failure` recovers an injected fixture failure pattern.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/prepare_change.rs` — redesigned `prepare_change` composing graph + event + memory + working-memory substrates into a one-call edit-planning bundle per spec §Phase 8.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/plan_edit.rs` — redesigned `plan_edit` producing ordered patch steps with stable-identity anchors, tests, docs updates, and verification commands.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/trace_scenario.rs` — redesigned `trace_scenario` walking call chains and attaching event/memory annotations.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/diagnose_failure.rs` — redesigned `diagnose_failure` matching failures against `FailurePattern` memory and prior `WorkflowFailed` events.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/edit_workflows_tests.rs` — unit + golden tests for each redesigned tool covering schema, stale-label discipline, event emission, hot-path budget, and recovery of fixture failure patterns.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/prepare_change.rs` — confirms the redesigned `prepare_change` file exists at the harness path.\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/plan_edit.rs` — confirms the redesigned `plan_edit` file exists at the harness path.\n- `cd daemon && cargo build --release` — the new workflow_v2 module compiles cleanly with the rest of the daemon.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-daemon --lib rpc::workflow_v2::edit_workflows_tests` — every edit-workflow test passes (schema, stale-label discipline, event emission, hot-path budget, failure-pattern recovery).\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines per file (split per-tool when needed; do not co-locate two redesigned tools in one file).\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10.\n- Schema parity: `WorkflowBundle` and per-tool request/response structs derive `Serialize`, `Deserialize`, `Debug`, `Clone` and every public field has a doc comment.\n- No silent error handling — every retrieval/verifier/event-writer failure returns a typed error and surfaces in the bundle as a `RiskNote` rather than being swallowed.\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code; no unjustified `#[allow(...)]`.\n- Public API names follow intent-over-mechanism naming (e.g. `MemoryHighlight::inclusion_reason`, not `MemoryHighlight::why_str`).\n- For SQLite: not applicable directly; storage access goes through Phase 2 event writer and Phase 3 memory store APIs, never raw SQL in this module.\n- Observability: every tool emits at least one `tracing::info!` span with `tool`, `task_id`, `session_id`, `bundle_size_bytes`, `event_count` fields per spec §MCP Tool Contract Principles.\n- Doc citation: cite spec headings `## Phase 8: Workflow Engine V2` and `## MCP Tool Contract Principles` in module doc comments where behavior is bound by those sections.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs).\n- [ ] Every verification command in tasks.json passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: every redesigned tool composes graph + event + memory + working-memory substrates in one call; no follow-up \"polish\" task is permitted to add the substrate composition later.\n- [ ] If a backward-incompatible change was needed, the AGENTS.md \"Backward-compatibility and contract discipline\" section was followed; legacy `prepare_change` / `plan_edit` / `trace_scenario` / `diagnose_failure` continue to respond per the T02 compatibility policy.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3831,"cache_read_input_tokens":55400,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3831,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_012n7S8LWZzY1cvitTHPzudV","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"05c46d50-b298-4f29-a42d-2dbcb0968787","request_id":"req_011Cb7MmdS4mZnDvp53Qjt6x","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 8+9+Gate task briefs"}
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T74.log:4052:docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T71.log:7951:docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T37.log:2062:docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T04.log:2718:./docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/00-decompose.log:660:{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_013ZXuTanJH7X6D7LHKK4aiQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VyFsJMQCiudocXkZ3sZYhd","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T07.md","content":"# T07 — Phase 1 — Identity resolver with ambiguity diagnostics\n\n**Phase:** 1\n**Type:** backend\n**Model class:** balanced\n**Depends on:** T06\n**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 1: Unified Identity Model](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-1-unified-identity-model)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task implements the resolver that turns user-supplied or LLM-supplied references — paths, qualified symbol names, doc headings, test names, event refs — into the stable `Identity` values defined in T06. Spec §Phase 1 names \"identity resolver for paths, symbols, headings, tests, and event refs\" as a deliverable and binds the resolver to return ambiguity diagnostics rather than arbitrary matches when an input has multiple candidate identities. Without this resolver, every later phase would re-implement name→id lookups inconsistently, and ambiguity would be silently swallowed.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Phase 1 Deliverables: ... identity resolver for paths, symbols, headings, tests, and event refs ... compatibility support for legacy name-based references.\"\n\n> \"Definition of done: every workflow output can be expanded through a stable identity; ambiguous names return ambiguity diagnostics instead of arbitrary matches.\"\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs: identity types from T06 (`daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/kinds.rs`, `encoding.rs`).\n- Existing files in the repo this task builds on:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/graph/` (workspace graph that backs path/symbol lookups)\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/storage/` (SQLite-backed lookups for files, symbols, docs, sections)\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/parser/` (doc heading and symbol extraction the resolver consumes)\n- Standards files to honor: `coding.md` hard limits, naming (intent over mechanism), error handling (resolver errors must be structured, never silent); `AGENTS.md` (resolver public API is binding once shipped — any change is a contract change).\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Create `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/resolver.rs` with a `pub struct IdentityResolver` that holds references to the graph, storage, and parser indexes needed to answer lookups.\n2. Define the resolver public API:\n   - `resolve_path(&self, workspace: &WorkspaceId, path: &str) -> Result<FileId, ResolveError>`\n   - `resolve_symbol(&self, workspace: &WorkspaceId, qualified_name: &str) -> ResolveOutcome<SymbolId>`\n   - `resolve_section(&self, workspace: &WorkspaceId, doc: &DocId, heading: &str) -> ResolveOutcome<SectionId>`\n   - `resolve_test(&self, workspace: &WorkspaceId, test_name: &str) -> ResolveOutcome<SymbolId>` (tests are identified as symbols with a `Test` kind)\n   - `resolve_event_ref(&self, workspace: &WorkspaceId, ref_str: &str) -> Result<EventId, ResolveError>`\n3. Create `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/ambiguity.rs` with the `ResolveOutcome<T>` enum (`Unique(T)`, `Ambiguous(AmbiguityReport<T>)`, `NotFound(ResolveError)`) and the `AmbiguityReport<T>` struct carrying the list of candidates plus a `disambiguation_hint` describing how the caller can narrow the query (suggest adding parent module, file path, byte offset, etc.).\n4. The resolver must never pick arbitrarily when multiple matches exist — return `Ambiguous`. Tests in T09 will assert this on duplicate symbol names.\n5. Add a legacy compatibility helper `pub fn resolve_legacy_symbol_name(&self, name: &str) -> ResolveOutcome<SymbolId>` that takes a name without workspace context and routes to the resolver via the default workspace, preserving older MCP payloads.\n6. Implement caching: keep a small LRU keyed by `(workspace, query)` so the same resolution within a session does not re-traverse the graph. Cache hits must still preserve ambiguity semantics — a cached `Ambiguous` returns `Ambiguous`.\n7. Errors are structured: `ResolveError::WorkspaceNotIndexed`, `ResolveError::Malformed`, `ResolveError::IndexLagBehind { latest_event_id }`. No bare `String` errors.\n8. Add module-level docs in both files citing spec §Phase 1.\n9. Register the new submodules in `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/mod.rs` with `pub mod resolver;` and `pub mod ambiguity;`.\n10. Write smoke unit tests inline (the full ambiguity / rename / branch-change test matrix is owned by T09): construct a tiny resolver fixture and assert `resolve_path` returns a `FileId`, `resolve_symbol` on a duplicate name returns `Ambiguous`, and `resolve_legacy_symbol_name` falls back correctly.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/resolver.rs` — `IdentityResolver` struct, the five `resolve_*` methods, LRU cache, structured `ResolveError`.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/ambiguity.rs` — `ResolveOutcome<T>`, `AmbiguityReport<T>`, `disambiguation_hint` helpers.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/resolver.rs` — confirms the resolver file exists.\n- `cd daemon && cargo build -p lattice-core` — confirms the crate compiles with the resolver and ambiguity modules wired into `lattice-core`.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib identity::resolver` — confirms the resolver smoke tests pass.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib identity::ambiguity` — confirms the ambiguity module tests pass.\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines (verify with `wc -l daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/resolver.rs daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/ambiguity.rs`).\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10 — every `resolve_*` method must fit; extract candidate-collection helpers if needed.\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code.\n- No unjustified `// allow(...)` or suppressions.\n- Public API names follow intent-over-mechanism naming (`resolve_symbol` not `lookup`, `AmbiguityReport` not `MultiResult`).\n- For schema changes: not applicable (resolver consumes existing storage).\n- Doc citation: cite the exact `## Phase 1: Unified Identity Model` heading from the spec in module docs; if any non-obvious caching or LRU choice is made, cite the heading from `docs/architecture/2026-04-11-stable-follow-up-handles.md` that authorizes the behavior (per `lattice/CLAUDE.md` § Markdown Heading References).\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs).\n- [ ] Every verification command in tasks.json passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: no item from spec §Phase 1 punted to a later phase.\n- [ ] If a backward-incompatible change was needed, the AGENTS.md \"Backward-compatibility and contract discipline\" section was followed and the architecture doc was updated in the same task.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":615,"cache_read_input_tokens":49571,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":615,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_016juPk15H1M5x3FpzubRVsP","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"1a20f582-7bfb-4d3c-8dba-826aa42e26d0","request_id":"req_011Cb7Mcwaxi2NndD8b7oC78","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 0+1 task briefs"}
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T74.log:4057:docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T71.log:7956:docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T37.log:2077:docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T04.log:2733:./docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/00-decompose.log:758:{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_019JjqMQ778TToFmau2PwXFQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TKbr7KNkKbifeCtRHe4Xvy","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T62.md","content":"# T62 — Phase 8 — Workflow outcome recording integrated by default + composition tests\n\n**Phase:** 8\n**Type:** tests\n**Model class:** balanced\n**Depends on:** T56, T57, T58, T59, T60, T61\n**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 8: Workflow Engine V2](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-8-workflow-engine-v2)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task wires automatic workflow-outcome recording into every redesigned tool from T56–T60 and ships the composition test suite that proves the new tools compose correctly over the underlying substrates. Spec §Phase 8 Deliverables names \"workflow outcome recording integrated by default\" as a binding deliverable. Spec §MCP Tool Contract Principles requires \"every workflow tool should record inputs, resolved anchors, selected candidates, excluded high-scoring candidates where useful, response summary, downstream use events.\" Without this task, individual tools work in isolation but the event log + memory consolidation cannot observe whether a workflow succeeded, which breaks Phase 6 procedure extraction and Phase 9 success metrics.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Phase 8 Deliverables: …workflow outcome recording integrated by default.\" (spec §Phase 8)\n\n> \"Every workflow tool should record: inputs; resolved anchors; selected candidates; excluded high-scoring candidates where useful; response summary; downstream use events.\" (spec §MCP Tool Contract Principles)\n\n> \"Required event types: …`WorkflowSucceeded`, `WorkflowFailed`…\" (spec §Event Log)\n\n> \"Definition of done: completed tasks produce useful episode memories; repeated successful traces produce procedural memories; consolidation is auditable, reversible, and test-covered.\" (spec §Phase 6 — depends on outcome capture from this task)\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs:\n  - T56 (`workflow_v2/` edit-planning tools).\n  - T57 (`workflow_v2/` discovery tools).\n  - T58–T60 (`memory_v2/` tools).\n  - T61 (final MCP tool reference).\n- Existing repo files this task builds on:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/events/` — Phase 2 event writer, including `WorkflowSucceeded` and `WorkflowFailed` envelopes.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/intelligence/record_workflow_outcome.rs` — current explicit outcome recorder, retained as a manual override path.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/` — every tool from T56/T57 to be wrapped with the outcome interceptor.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/` — every tool from T58/T59/T60 to be wrapped with the outcome interceptor.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/session_metrics.rs` — outcome events feed session metrics.\n- Standards: Cadres coding standard §Hard limits, §Single source of truth, §No broken windows, §Schema parity, §Observability, §Tests as documentation; Lattice rules on Markdown heading references.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read spec §Phase 8, §MCP Tool Contract Principles, and §Event Log in full. Quote the \"Every workflow tool should record…\" paragraph verbatim into a doc comment on `workflow_v2/outcome_capture.rs` so the contract is enforced at the call site.\n2. Implement `workflow_v2/outcome_capture.rs` as a reusable interceptor: a `WorkflowOutcomeRecorder` type that wraps any tool handler, captures inputs, resolved anchors, selected candidates, excluded candidates (the top-N high-scoring candidates that were rejected and why), response summary, and emits a `WorkflowSucceeded` or `WorkflowFailed` event on completion. The recorder must run on the hot path within the spec §Phase 2 budget (≤5ms P99 overhead).\n3. Wire `WorkflowOutcomeRecorder` into every redesigned tool from T56 and T57 by default. Wire it into every memory tool from T58/T59/T60 that participates in a user-facing workflow (excluding `get_event_trace`, which would create a feedback loop). Default-on means the tool registration in `mcp.rs` constructs the recorder around the handler; the legacy explicit `record_workflow_outcome` tool remains available as a manual override per the T02 compatibility policy.\n4. The recorder must also feed `session_metrics` so success rate, irrelevant-files-opened, and `workflow_success_after_first_plan` (from spec §Phase 9) are accumulated automatically.\n5. Define how \"downstream use events\" are tracked: when a returned context handle or memory ID is subsequently referenced in another tool call, the recorder back-links the later event to the originating workflow via the Phase 2 `EventEnvelope::references` field.\n6. In `workflow_v2/composition_tests.rs`, write composition tests that exercise the new tools end-to-end against a fixture workspace: (a) `prepare_change → plan_edit → apply_patch_simulated → record outcome` chain emits the correct sequence of events; (b) `get_context_capsule → expand_context` chain returns stable handle deltas without redundant payload; (c) `diagnose_failure → prepare_change` chain reuses anchors from the failure diagnosis; (d) `save_memory → verify_explain_memory` chain transitions an unverified memory to a verified state and emits the matching events; (e) `consolidate_session → propose_memory_evolution(action=\"apply\")` chain applies a proposal that the session produced; (f) every workflow chain emits exactly one `WorkflowSucceeded` or `WorkflowFailed` event per outer call; (g) excluded high-scoring candidates appear in the recorded outcome with rejection reasons.\n7. Assert that the hot-path budget is honored: composition tests measure the per-tool overhead added by `WorkflowOutcomeRecorder` and fail if it exceeds the spec §Phase 2 ≤5ms P99 budget.\n8. Assert that scope-leak and workspace-boundary protections from T58–T60 are preserved when the recorder is in the path.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/outcome_capture.rs` — `WorkflowOutcomeRecorder` interceptor capturing inputs, resolved anchors, selected/excluded candidates, response summary, and emitting `WorkflowSucceeded` / `WorkflowFailed` events per spec §MCP Tool Contract Principles; wired by default into every T56–T60 tool.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/composition_tests.rs` — end-to-end composition tests covering chained tool calls, handle stability, anchor reuse, verification transitions, consolidation→apply chains, outcome emission, excluded-candidate recording, and hot-path budget.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/outcome_capture.rs` — confirms the recorder file exists at the harness path.\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/composition_tests.rs` — confirms the composition test file exists at the harness path.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-daemon --lib rpc::workflow_v2::composition_tests` — every composition test passes (event ordering, handle stability, anchor reuse, verification transition, consolidation→apply, excluded-candidate recording, hot-path budget, scope-leak preservation).\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines per file.\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10.\n- Schema parity: the recorded outcome payload uses the same `WorkflowSucceeded` / `WorkflowFailed` envelopes defined in Phase 2; no parallel outcome struct is introduced.\n- No silent error handling — recorder failures emit `tracing::warn!` AND surface as `RiskNote`s in the bundle, never swallowed.\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code; no unjustified `#[allow(...)]`.\n- Public API names follow intent-over-mechanism naming (`WorkflowOutcomeRecorder::record_excluded`, not `WorkflowOutcomeRecorder::also_excl`).\n- For SQLite: outcome persistence goes through the Phase 2 event writer; no raw SQL in the RPC layer.\n- Observability: the recorder emits one `tracing::info!` span per recorded outcome with `tool`, `task_id`, `session_id`, `outcome`, `excluded_count`, `latency_ms` fields.\n- Doc citation: cite spec headings `## Phase 8: Workflow Engine V2`, `## MCP Tool Contract Principles`, `## Event Log`, and `## Phase 2 — Event Log Substrate` Definition of Done (hot-path budget) in module doc comments.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs).\n- [ ] Every verification command in tasks.json passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: the recorder is wired by default into every T56–T60 tool eligible for outcome capture; composition tests cover every chained scenario named in the steps; the hot-path budget assertion is live, not commented out.\n- [ ] If a backward-incompatible change was needed, the AGENTS.md \"Backward-compatibility and contract discipline\" section was followed; the legacy explicit `record_workflow_outcome` tool continues to respond per the T02 compatibility policy.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3649,"cache_read_input_tokens":81273,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3649,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":54,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_012n7S8LWZzY1cvitTHPzudV","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"729bf2f0-fa94-4854-a179-85471920cbc3","request_id":"req_011Cb7NBPjimQ7hZ8gS7hpnH","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 8+9+Gate task briefs"}
